  "Section heading. 'Rich text' = text with links/emphasis; 'slot tags' = the [name] bracket placeholders ng-linguo uses in translations\u0004Rich text (slot tags)": "Rich text (slot tags)",
  "Card title. The point: links and styled text appear in the UI, but the translation files stay plain text with no HTML\u0004Links and bold text — with no HTML in your translation files": "Links and bold text — with no HTML in your translation files",
  "Card body. 'named slots' = the [name] bracket placeholders; keep 'ng-template tFor' verbatim; 'real bracket' = a literal [ character; 'XSS' is the web-security term (keep). [[name]…[[/name] is escaped so it shows as the literal text [name]…[/name] — keep the doubled brackets\u0004Translators only ever see named slots like [[name]…[[/name] — never HTML tags. You bind each slot to your own ng-template tFor, so you decide what it renders as: a link, bold text, anything. Need a real bracket in your text? Type the opening one twice. Translated text is never inserted as HTML, so cross-site scripting (XSS) is impossible by design.": "Translators only ever see named slots like [[name]…[[/name] — never HTML tags. You bind each slot to your own ng-template tFor, so you decide what it renders as: a link, bold text, anything. Need a real bracket in your text? Type the opening one twice. Translated text is never inserted as HTML, so cross-site scripting (XSS) is impossible by design.",
  "Onboarding hint. [docs] wraps a link to the documentation — translate the wrapped word too and keep the [docs] tags around it\u0004Read the [docs]documentation[/docs] to get started": "Read the [docs]documentation[/docs] to get started",
  "Consent line shown before sign-up. [terms] wraps a link; 'Terms of Service' is the standard name of the legal agreement — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004By continuing you agree to our [terms]Terms of Service[/terms]": "By continuing you agree to our [terms]Terms of Service[/terms]",
  "Warning before a destructive, irreversible action. [warn] wraps the emphasized lead word 'Warning:'\u0004[warn]Warning:[/warn] this action cannot be undone": "[warn]Warning:[/warn] this action cannot be undone",
  "Demo of ng-linguo's slot syntax and its bracket escape. 'Escaped' is the programming sense (made literal via the [[ escape), not fleeing; 'stays literal' = shown as plain text; 'slot' = a fillable [name] region. [[b]bold[[/b] is escaped literal text, [b]this[/b] is a real slot — keep both forms exactly\u0004Escaped [[b]bold[[/b] stays literal — [b]this[/b] is a slot": "Escaped [[b]bold[[/b] stays literal — [b]this[/b] is a slot",
  "Consent line with a nested slot. [link] wraps a link to the Terms; [b] emphasizes a word inside it. 'Terms and Conditions' is the standard legal-document name — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004Agree to our [link]Terms and [b]Conditions[/b][/link]": "Agree to our [link]Terms and [b]Conditions[/b][/link]",
  "Section-group label: the surrounding workflow — the ESLint setup and the extract/translate/compile pipeline\u0004Tooling & workflow": "Tooling & workflow",
  "Section heading. 'ESLint' is a tool name — keep verbatim; 'a11y' is the numeronym for accessibility (keep, or use the target word for accessibility)\u0004ESLint & a11y": "ESLint & a11y",
  "Card title (colloquial). 'accessibility linter' = the ESLint a11y rule; 'keep it happy' = satisfy the rule; '[t]' is a code symbol (keep); 'empty elements' = elements with no text written in the HTML\u0004Keep the accessibility linter happy with empty [t] elements": "Keep the accessibility linter happy with empty [t] elements",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: @angular-eslint/template/elements-content, [t]. 'markup' = the HTML you write; 'fallback' = text shown before translations load; 'the hero' = the large heading at the top of the page\u0004Angular's accessibility rule @angular-eslint/template/elements-content warns about empty headings, links, and buttons. A [t] element gets its text at runtime, so you can leave the markup empty — every heading on this page is an empty [t] element, and only the hero keeps its text as a fallback shown before translations load.": "Angular's accessibility rule @angular-eslint/template/elements-content warns about empty headings, links, and buttons. A [t] element gets its text at runtime, so you can leave the markup empty — every heading on this page is an empty [t] element, and only the hero keeps its text as a fallback shown before translations load.",
  "Section heading: the build-time CLI pipeline that turns source strings into translated files (extract, translate, compile)\u0004Translation workflow": "Translation workflow",
  "Card title. 'English source' = the original strings; 'translated files' = the per-language .po/.json files\u0004From English source to translated files": "From English source to translated files",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: extract CLI, gettext, .po, JSON, ng-linguo, SDK, API key, translator, CI. 'additive' = re-running adds without overwriting; 'guided menu' = the interactive CLI; 'chat model' = an LLM such as ChatGPT/Gemini/Claude; 'merges the reply' = applies the model's response back into the files\u0004The extract CLI scans your source, keeps the strings in standard gettext .po files, and compiles them to the JSON the app loads. Re-running it is additive — new strings merge in, existing translations stay. Run it with no command for a guided menu, or as plain commands in CI. To translate, copy a ready-made prompt into any chat model, or point the translator option at a small module that calls your own AI provider — ng-linguo writes the prompt and merges the reply, and your SDK and API key never leave your machine.": "The extract CLI scans your source, keeps the strings in standard gettext .po files, and compiles them to the JSON the app loads. Re-running it is additive — new strings merge in, existing translations stay. Run it with no command for a guided menu, or as plain commands in CI. To translate, copy a ready-made prompt into any chat model, or point the translator option at a small module that calls your own AI provider — ng-linguo writes the prompt and merges the reply, and your SDK and API key never leave your machine.",
  "Page footer. 'ng-linguo' is the product name (keep verbatim); 'living documentation' = documentation that is also a working demo\u0004Built with ng-linguo · this playground is also living documentation.": "Built with ng-linguo · this playground is also living documentation.",
